/**
 * Charges the losses of the electricity network over the days `from` to `to` (both included) per node of the
 * meter tree (substation and quarter meters that had a meter under them on a day of the range), money rules
 * section 6. The range consumption of a meter is its end-of-day value on `to` minus its end-of-day value on the
 * day before `from` (`valueAt(to) - valueAt(from - 1)`), with the tree as it was on each day. For every node:
 * losses = the node's consumption - the consumption of its children (plot meters, common consumers, quarter
 * meters) over the days they were under it; the losses are shared among the plots under the node (directly or
 * through child nodes) in proportion to each plot's consumption under it, a plot with zero consumption gets
 * nothing. Each plot's kWh from every node are added and priced once with the plot's electricity tariff (`PER_KWH`,
 * split by days when the rate changes) and rounded once: one `LOSSES` charge per plot per run, booked in the month
 * of `to` (or the earliest open month after it when that month is closed), with the debt counting from `to`.
 * Outcomes per node: `CHARGED`; `NEGATIVE` (the children used more than the node shows: nothing is charged);
 * `UNKNOWN` (a value of the node or of a child is unknown, no reading after the range end: the node is skipped);
 * `SKIPPED_ABOVE` (a node below is unknown: skipped too); `ALREADY_CHARGED` (a booked run charged the node for a
 * day of the range). Values calculated between readings are allowed and marked `calculated`. `nodeIds` limits
 * the run to those nodes (absent or empty: every node); the other nodes are still calculated where a selected node
 * needs them but are not listed. With `preview=true` nothing is written and the answer has a `digest`. With
 * `preview=false` the run is booked: the run and its nodes are stored, the charges written, each `UNKNOWN` or
 * `SKIPPED_ABOVE` node gets a "not charged" item (`LOSSES_NODE`, `UNKNOWN_NODE_VALUE`), the open items of a node
 * that is now charged are closed, and the meter values the charged nodes read can no longer be corrected while the
 * run is booked. Field codes of 400 `VALIDATION_FAILED`: `to` `INVALID` (before `from`) or `DATE_IN_FUTURE` (after
 * today in Europe/Kyiv); `nodeIds[i]` `NOT_FOUND` (not a node of the tree in the range). Conflicts (409): the
 * losses mode of the cooperative is not `PROPORTIONAL` (`LOSSES_MODE_NOT_PROPORTIONAL`, preview too); a booking
 * with a selected node that is `ALREADY_CHARGED` (`LOSSES_RANGE_OVERLAP`; book the other nodes with `nodeIds`);
 * a booking with the `digest` of a preview that no longer matches (`PREVIEW_OUTDATED`; the digest covers the
 * listed nodes that are not `ALREADY_CHARGED` and the charges, so a preview of every node matches a booking of
 * those nodes). Requires `CHARGES_RUN`; a booking is written to the audit log (`LOSSES_RUN_BOOKED`, entity type
 * `LOSSES_RUN`, label `from/to`, values `from`, `to`, `billingMonth`, `nodes`, `count`, `total`).
 * @summary Preview or book a proportional losses run
 */
